  "scope": "Stage4J7: D3D9 final state cleanup starts only when total public device refs reach zero. An externally referenced2D/cube/volume/VB/IB/declaration/VS/PS or completed stateblock preserves every live binding and scalar state after the last direct device Release. Recording blocks have no public parent pin; End adds exactly one before publishing, public block destruction releases it last. Final release still cancels unfinished recording and drains internal bindings under callback protection. Actual native methods with constructor/scalar stubs:111616 new checks,2048 pool/anchor/final-owner profiles and2048 actual GetDevice recoveries,eight anchors,full binding and scalar preservation,pending recording retention and final device/anchor/block orders.9 strict assertion mutants,two old actual Device.Release/End controls,ASAN/UBSAN; all retained graph and private-callback suites. XP exercises each of eight resource families as the only public child pin with no CPU surface during the critical Release. It then recovers device through that child,checks eight exact identities/offset/stride,cull and shader constants,and draws. Ninth device cancels unfinished internal recording with no parent pin; tenth device is retained only by a completed public stateblock,recovers through its GetDevice and draws.80 resources,10 logical devices,72 binding getter queries,nine metadata rounds,20 exact uploads,83 bindings,nine custom constants/nine real readbacks. Simulated XP replies prove transport only; dual GPU independently checks576 pixels and complete80-resource/10-device cleanup before owner release. ZENABLE uses the shared creation default(false without auto-depth) because repeated guest setters are suppressed. D3D8,NULL-stream offset/stride retail quirks,arbitrary callbacks/thread/loss/full Reset/format/MSAA/fullscreen/multi-buffer/wrapper conversion,native HAL,games/FPS and overall stages4/5/6 remain open. Host/protocol/shader/bundle and D3D8/DDraw unchanged.",
